{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<figure class=\"table\"><table border=\"1\"><caption>Data Set Q</caption>\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 50%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\" scope=\"col\">Value</th>\n<th style=\"width: 50%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\" scope=\"col\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"110\"><mn>110</mn>\n</math></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"30\"><mn>30</mn>\n</math></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 22.3906px; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></figure>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<figure class=\"table\"><table border=\"1\"><caption>Data Set R</caption>\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 50.1567%; height: 22.3906px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" scope=\"col\">Value</th>\n<th style=\"width: 50%; height: 22.3906px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" scope=\"col\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 50.1567%; height: 22.3906px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 22.3906px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 50.1567%; height: 22.3906px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 22.3906px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 50.1567%; height: 22.3906px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 22.3906px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"11\"><mn>11</mn>\n</math></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></figure>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Data sets Q and R are summarized in the tables shown, where <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> are positive, consecutive integers and <math alttext=\"a less than b less than c\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi></math>. Which statement comparing the means of the data sets is true?</p>", "keys": ["11cbe562-f3c3-4b89-8920-fcc9ef039071"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "d8e461db-d3e3-4bec-b8ce-f16b3d40b7dc", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The mean of data set R is <math alttext=\"StartFraction 2 left parenthesis 11 right parenthesis Over 14 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mn>11</mn></mfenced></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math> less than the mean of data set Q.</p>"}, {"id": "11cbe562-f3c3-4b89-8920-fcc9ef039071", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The mean of data set R is <math alttext=\"StartFraction 2 left parenthesis 11 right parenthesis Over 14 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mn>11</mn></mfenced></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math> greater than the mean of data set Q.</p>"}, {"id": "9f536665-306b-48d7-87a2-dd253d3e23ff", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The mean of data set Q is <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> times the mean of data set R.</p>"}, {"id": "cda45fea-bf74-42d2-9c62-4dc48a8a2e2b", "content": "<p>The means of the two data sets are equal.</p>"}], "rationale": "<p>Choice B is correct. The mean of a data set is the sum of the values of the data set divided by the total number of values in the data set. When a data set is represented in a frequency table, the sum of the values in the data set is the sum of the products of each value and its frequency. For data set Q, the sum of the products of each value and its frequency is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"110 a plus 30 b plus 0 c\"><mn>110</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>c</mi></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"110 a plus 30 b\"><mn>110</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>b</mi></math>, and the number of values is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"110 plus 30 plus 0\"><mn>110</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"140\"><mn>140</mn></math>. Therefore, the mean of data set Q is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 110 a plus 30 b Over 140 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>110</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow><mn>140</mn></mfrac></math>. For data set R, the sum of the products of each value and its frequency is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0 a plus 3 b plus 11 c\"><mn>0</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>c</mi></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3 b plus 11 c\"><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>c</mi></math>, and the number of values is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0 plus 3 plus 11\"><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn></math>. Therefore, the mean of data set R is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 3 b plus 11 c Over 14 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>c</mi></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math>. Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> are positive, consecutive integers and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a less than b less than c\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>c</mi></math>, it follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b equals a plus 1\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c equals a plus 2\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a plus 1\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> in the mean of data set Q yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 110 a plus 30 left parenthesis a plus 1 right parenthesis Over 140 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>110</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>140</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 110 a plus 30 a plus 30 Over 140 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>110</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><mn>140</mn></mfrac></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 140 a plus 30 Over 140 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>140</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><mn>140</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a plus three fourteenths\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a plus 1\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a plus 2\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> in the mean of data set R yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 3 left parenthesis a plus 1 right parenthesis plus 11 left parenthesis a plus 2 right parenthesis Over 14 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 3 a plus 3 plus 11 a plus 2 left parenthesis 11 right parenthesis Over 14 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math>, which is equivalent to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 14 a plus 3 plus 2 left parenthesis 11 right parenthesis Over 14 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>14</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a plus three fourteenths plus StartFraction 2 left parenthesis 11 right parenthesis Over 14 EndFraction\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>14</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math>. Subtracting the mean of data set Q from the mean of data set R yields&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis a plus three fourteenths plus StartFraction 2 left parenthesis 11 right parenthesis Over 14 EndFraction right parenthesis minus left parenthesis a plus three fourteenths right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>14</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>14</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 2 left parenthesis 11 right parenthesis Over 14 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, the mean of data set R is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 2 left parenthesis 11 right parenthesis Over 14 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math> greater than the mean of data set Q.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "46b54ee4-c738-4f84-acf0-ed71e853d400", "correct_answer": ["B"]}